* Minimoog board No. 3: circuit No. 3, the noise generator (white, pink and red noise).
*
* Source drawing: service manual Figure 9-8 (S-F98); reference designators are Figure 9-8's.
* The circuit runs between +10 V (pin 1) and -10 V (pins 17, 18).
*
* The noise source is Q15's emitter-base junction in reverse breakdown ("selected,
* burned-in and retested", 2.5), fed from +10 V through R47 75K (decoupled by C25 10 uF)
* and R67 470K, its collector open. Its noise is not in any netlist: here the junction is a
* voltage source `src` (its breakdown voltage, and the noise as its AC value) behind its
* small-signal resistance `rd` (docs/circuit/board3.md). Q12 amplifies it (R26, NOISE LEVEL,
* the factory's trim for "-5dB", sets its gain), Q4 follows: white noise out through C18.
* R16 into two series RC branches to -10 V (C3 with R8, C2 with R13) filters that into Q3
* (gain R3/R1): pink noise out through C20.
* R12 and C7 filter that into Q6 (C22 on its collector): red noise out through C28, R59.
*
* Ports: white (pin 5), pink (pin 6), red (pin 2), p10 (+10 V), n10 (-10 V).
* Parameters: r26 (NOISE LEVEL, ohm in circuit, 0..2.5K), vbr (the junction's breakdown
* voltage), rd (its small-signal resistance), acn (the noise source's AC value).
.subckt mm_noise white pink red p10 n10 params: r26=1250 vbr=7.5 rd=1k acn=1
* --- the noise source ----------------------------------------------------------------------
r47   p10 nx 75k                    ; R47 75K
c25   nx n10 10u                    ; C25 10 uF
r67   nx e15 470k                   ; R67 470K
vq15  jq n10 dc {vbr} ac {acn}      ; Q15's emitter-base junction in breakdown (base at -10 V)
rq15  jq e15 {rd}
* --- Q12: amplifier; Q4: follower ----------------------------------------------------------
c12   e15 b12 5.6u                  ; C12 5.6 uF
r29   b12 c12n 4.7meg               ; R29 4.7M
r17   p10 c12n 100k                 ; R17 100K
c11   c12n n10 100p                 ; C11 100 pF
q12   c12n b12 e12 Q2N3392          ; Q12 2N3392
r26   e12 n10 {max(r26,1e-3)}       ; R26 2.5K NOISE LEVEL (a rheostat)
q4    c4 c12n e4 Q2N3392            ; Q4 2N3392
r9    p10 c4 470                    ; R9 470
r19   e4 n10 3.3k                   ; R19 3.3K
c5    c12n e4 100p                  ; C5 100 pF
c18   e4 white 0.15u                ; C18 .15 uF: white noise out
* --- the pink filter and Q3 ---------------------------------------------------------------
r16   e4 p1 10k                     ; R16 10K
c3    p1 n3 0.12u                   ; C3 .12 uF, in series with
r8    n3 n10 3.3k                   ; R8 3.3K
c2    p1 n2 0.033u                  ; C2 .033 uF
r13   n2 n10 220                    ; R13 220
c1    p1 b3 2.5u                    ; C1 2.5 uF
r7    b3 y3 560k                    ; R7 560K
r6    y3 c3n 560k                   ; R6 560K
c4    y3 n10 2.5u                   ; C4 2.5 uF
q3    c3n b3 e3 Q2N3392             ; Q3 2N3392
r3    p10 c3n 3.3k                  ; R3 3.3K
r1    e3 n10 120                    ; R1 120
c20   c3n pink 2.5u                 ; C20 2.5 uF: pink noise out
* --- the red filter and Q6 ----------------------------------------------------------------
r12   c3n r1n 10k                   ; R12 10K
c7    r1n n10 0.15u                 ; C7 .15 uF
c8    r1n b6 2.5u                   ; C8 2.5 uF
r28   b6 z6 2.2meg                  ; R28 2.2M
r23   z6 c6n 2.2meg                 ; R23 2.2M
c10   z6 n10 0.1u                   ; C10 .1 uF
q6    c6n b6 e6 Q2N3392             ; Q6 2N3392
r24   p10 c6n 10k                   ; R24 10K
r15   e6 n10 3.9k                   ; R15 3.9K
c22   c6n n10 0.15u                 ; C22 .15 uF
c28   c6n red 10u                   ; C28 10 uF: red noise out
r59   red 0 100k                    ; R59 100K
.ends mm_noise
